      "selection": "The readings, the disc swelling, the systemic symptoms, the arrangements and the safety advice are kept. Detailed fundus signs, pressures, near vision and lifestyle detail such as night work and diet are left out or reduced, as the hospital and GP will take their own history.",
      "organisation": "Purpose, then findings, then what has been done and safety-netting, then risk factors, then the specific requests and review.",
      "tone": "Clear and serious without alarm; the eye findings are framed as evidence of a medical emergency rather than an eye problem."
