      "selection": "The capacity assessment and the fact that this is his decision are given prominence because they are the legal basis social care must understand. The covert thickening is raised as a possible safeguarding concern because social work must decide on it. The trial-by-trial swallow results are condensed, and the full history is left out as not needed by social work.",
      "organisation": "Purpose, then the risk and the capacity decision, then what staff must do, then the safeguarding question, then monitoring, escalation and review.",
      "tone": "Clear and respectful of the client's autonomy, firm on the protective measures and on the covert thickening that must not recur."
